READ"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mx-auto mt-12 flex max-w-[1040px] flex-col gap-12 md:mt-16 xl:mt-16 xl:px-10","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-heading text-[28px] font-semibold leading-[36px] tracking-[-0.1296px] text-black md:text-[32px] md:leading-[40px] xl:text-[36px] xl:leading-[44px]","children":"Smart Home Integration: Motorized Shades 101"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-12","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"flex flex-col gap-8 xl:flex-row xl:gap-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-[23px] text-[16px] leading-[23px] text-navy xl:w-[425px] xl:shrink-0","children":[["$","p","Motorized window shades have e",{"children":"Motorized window shades have evolved from a luxury feature to an increasingly standard component of modern Florida homes. Today's systems integrate seamlessly with popular smart home platforms, offering convenience, energy savings, and enhanced security."}],["$","p","Whether you're building a new ",{"children":"Whether you're building a new home, renovating, or simply upgrading your existing window treatments, understanding the options available helps you make an informed investment."}],["$","p","This guide covers everything f",{"children":"This guide covers everything from basic motorization concepts to advanced smart home integration, helping you decide what's right for your lifestyle and budget."}],["$","p","Let's start with the fundament",{"children":"Let's start with the fundamentals."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative aspect-[4/3] w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg xl:flex-1 xl:self-stretch xl:aspect-auto","children":["$","$Lf",null,{"src":"https://www.figma.com/api/mcp/asset/ee8e1302-c513-4fff-a95e-6a569cb2228b.png","alt":"Smart home control panel for motorized shades","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}]]}],"$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15","$L16","$L17"]}]]}]]}]]}]
